    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Homotopy_lifting_lemma_unique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lift_HT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">homo_lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₂</span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Homotopy_lifting_lemma_ext</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lift_HT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">homo_lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think this might be the one.</p>",
        "id": 506504489,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruize Chen",
        "timestamp": 1742309893
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think I'd aim for the more general result that if one has a free and properly discontinuous action of a group G on a topological space X, then one gets a covering map (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/7596\">#7596</a>) <code>X → X / G</code> that is Galois (i.e. the range of the induced map between fundamental groups is a normal subgroup; it's known from <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/22649\">#22649</a> that the map is injective). Using the mechanism of monodromy in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/22771\">#22771</a> we should be able to show that G is isomorphic to the quotient <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(X/G)/\\pi_1(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. Now if X is the real line and G is the subgroup of integers, then X/G is the circle and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(X)=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, so we get the isomorphism <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(X/G)\\cong G\\cong\\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span></span></span></span>. Notice that <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/7596\">#7596</a> doesn't require the target to be X/G and can work with any quotient map.</p>",
        "id": 506514971,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1742312433
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is basically done in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/33108\">#33108</a>. Observations from working out the details: the map <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(X/G)/\\pi_1(X)\\to G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> more naturally goes into <code>Gᵐᵒᵖ</code> and different choices of a base point in a fiber (a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-torsor) lead to maps differing by conjugation; if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> is abelian there's only one canonical map. The action of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(X/G)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is basically \"right multiplication\" on a <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>-torsor.<br>\nUnfortunately I'll be traveling for the next two weeks and may not have the time to finish and clean up until the trip ends.</p>",
        "id": 564787599,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1766186464
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm delighted report that we merged <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/33108\">#33108</a> today and so in principle it should be trivial for us to prove that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_1(S^1) = \\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>In practice I have just realised that to do so (in a sane way), we really need the additive version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsQuotientCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquiv#doc\">docs#IsQuotientCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquiv</a> (this link won't work until the next run of doc_gen but the lemma is in master).</p>",
        "id": 604905005,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1781879272
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The relevant snippet is:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.Lifting</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">#check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCircle.isAddQuotientCoveringMap_coe</span>\n<span class=\"k\">#check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle.isAddQuotientCoveringMap_exp</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Argh, no additive version</span>\n<span class=\"k\">#check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsQuotientCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquiv</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FundamentalGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UnitAddCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiplicative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FundamentalGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiplicative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 604905147,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1781879305
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I mention this here in case it might motivate someone to take this on. We're <em>very</em> close to the fundamental group of the circle now.</p>",
        "id": 604905453,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1781879368
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Mentioning that some parts of this are in the PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36119\">#36119</a>, but maybe that's sufficiently out-of-date now.</p>",
        "id": 604906027,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1781879482
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for taking care of my PR!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>we really need the additive version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsQuotientCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquiv#doc\">docs#IsQuotientCoveringMap.fundamentalGroupEquiv</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Given an AddAction of some group G on a space, my approach would be to define a MulAction of <code>Multiplicative G</code> on the same space, and show <code>IsAddQuotientCoveringMap f G</code> is equivalent to <code>IsQuotientCoveringMap f (Multiplicative G)</code>, which can then be used to transfer the results.</p>",
        "id": 604919171,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1781882205
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40947\">#40947</a> to implement the above plan.</p>",
        "id": 605997791,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1782219996
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To be sure this is enough, I also verified that the following works on that branch:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.Lifting</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Contractible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- For `SimplyConnectedSpace ℝ`. Add shortcut?</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Thanks Junyan!</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsAddTorsionFree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup.zmultiples</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">zmultiplesHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofInjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">injective_iff_map_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsAddTorsionFree.zsmul_eq_zero_iff_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FundamentalGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UnitAddCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiplicative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">AddCircle.isAddQuotientCoveringMap_coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fundamentalGroupEquiv</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">⟩)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MulEquiv.inv'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm.trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one_ne_zero</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMultiplicative</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baz</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FundamentalGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Circle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiplicative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Circle.isAddQuotientCoveringMap_exp.fundamentalGroupEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">⟩)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MulEquiv.inv'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm.trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_num</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMultiplicative</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 605997905,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1782220024
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for taking on the additivization, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"240862\">@Oliver Nash</span> - cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"224323\">@Junyan Xu</span>. Once <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40947\">#40947</a> lands I'll follow up with the circle result on top of <code>fundamentalGroupEquiv</code>: constructing <code>nsmulLoop</code> and proving its image under the isomorphism is <code>n</code>, then packaging <code>FundamentalGroup UnitAddCircle 0 ≃* Multiplicative ℤ</code> and <code>FundamentalGroup Circle 1 ≃* Multiplicative ℤ</code>.</p>",
        "id": 606035536,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruize Chen",
        "timestamp": 1782228847
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>ℤ ≃+ AddSubgroup.zmultiples p</code> can be obtained from <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Subgroup/Ker.html#AddMonoidHom.ofInjective\">AddMonoidHom.ofInjective</a> applied to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=zmultiplesHom#doc\">docs#zmultiplesHom</a>; the slight defeq abuse could be removed by redefining <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Subgroup/ZPowers/Basic.html#AddSubgroup.zmultiples\">AddSubgroup.zmultiples</a> to be (abbrev of) the range of zmultiplesHom.<br>\nThis works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zmultiples</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">zmultiplesHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofInjective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">injective_iff_map_eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">IsAddTorsionFree</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zsmul_eq_zero_iff_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mp</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 606116911,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1782258367
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>is SimplyConnectedSpace (𝕊ⁿ) for n ≥ 2 on anyone's roadmap? it's a missing piece for e.g. π₁(ℝPⁿ) ≃ ℤ/2</p>",
        "id": 611223896,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1784272174
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/28246\">#28246</a></p>",
        "id": 611224023,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1784272239
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>awesome, glad it's in flight!</p>",
        "id": 611225625,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1784272928
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hmmm... what about: T² = S¹ × S¹ ( ℝⁿ/ℤⁿ  already exists via <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40947\">#40947</a>) and the theorem π₁(X × Y) ≃ π₁(X) × π₁(Y), not for groupoids but for groups? Nice extension of  π₁(S¹) = ℤ?</p>",
        "id": 611226156,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1784273141
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, and for T² (or Tⁿ generally) you don't even need the product theorem </p>\n<p>I'm finishing the circle PR now, <code>windingNumberIso</code> together with the computation that <code>nsmulLoop n</code> has winding number <code>n</code>, and plan to look at Tⁿ right after.</p>",
        "id": 611230643,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruize Chen",
        "timestamp": 1784274844
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The circle PR is up: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41856\">#41856</a> (<code>π₁(AddCircle 1) ≃* Multiplicative ℤ</code>, plus the winding number computation).</p>",
        "id": 611260894,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruize Chen",
        "timestamp": 1784285433
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Very neat! I will check it out :)</p>",
        "id": 611294689,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1784296149
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I may have to dust off my copy of Hatcher and see what I can add. This would be a fun project.</p>",
        "id": 611310981,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Korbonits",
        "timestamp": 1784300651
    }
]